<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Justin I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 450–527 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Justin I was a Byzantine emperor of the early sixth century, uncle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/justinian-i">Justinian I</a>. According to the site, a major Aksumite naval expedition across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-sea">Red Sea</a> was undertaken at his request. It defeated the Himyarite king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dhu-nuwas">Dhu Nuwas</a> and extended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aksumite-empire">Aksumite Empire</a>'s control over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-arabia">South Arabia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/justin-i.jpg" alt="Justin I" width="320" height="308" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Solidus_of_Justin_I_(obverse).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
